WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.780
Launches are ongoing across Europe and the Middle East.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.720
And we'll see further expansion in the second half post the EMEA, Japan, and Swiss approvals.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:16.860
Now, importantly, in chronic inducible urticaria, we presented our REMIND data supporting remibrutinib

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.980
as the potential as the first targeted therapy for chronic inducible urticaria.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:29.420
We had early and broad efficacy with onset as early as week two in the two additional largest subtypes,

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.220
consistent 12-week responses versus placebo.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:40.400
So we're on track for the FDA approval in SD, which is the most common Sindhu subtype,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.940
two-thirds of Sindhu patients.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.040
And then we'll have global filings across all three subtypes later this year.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:52.180
Just as a reminder, we estimate in the U.S. there's about 100,000 Sindhu patients

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.420
that are uncontrolled with antihistamines with no other treatment options.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:02.460
So this is a significant expansion in the population that can be helped by Rapsido.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.060
Now, turning to slide 14, we also presented some updated data on Yonalimab,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.860
showing the favorable SI benefits of the medicine and longer-term follow-up.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.020
And we remain on track for a U.S. launch in Stogen's disease,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.280
in the second half.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.840
So you can see on the left-hand side of this chart, in our pooled Neptunus data,

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:27.280
you can see the consistent benefits in SDI, statistically significant,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.040
versus the placebo arm across both studies when pooled,

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.320
demonstrating the benefits we see with the medicine.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.180
And then, as well, we presented 108-week long-term extension data,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.920
which showed that we can maintain the benefits of Yonalimab over time,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.640
and it also was supported by clinically meaningful improvements

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.200
for the placebo crossover group when crossing over onto the active arm.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.620
Also, throughout all of these long-term follow-ups,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.260
we see a favorable safety profile, no increase in adverse events.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.200
So this supports Yonalimab's multi-blockbuster potential.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.240
We're on track for the ITP first-line readout in the second half of 2026.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.420
